  "id": "Compound::DB01167 - Gene::1551",
  "verbalization": "Itraconazole is linked to Cyp3a7 through multiple pathways that collectively suggest a role in the regulation of this enzyme. The evidence indicates that Itraconazole, as an antifungal agent, binds to Cyp3a7-cyp3a51p, which in turn is bound by clotrimazole. Clotrimazole, an azole antifungal, directly binds to Cyp3a7, establishing a chain of interactions that connects Itraconazole to the enzyme. This suggests that Itraconazole may influence Cyp3a7 through its interaction with clotrimazole, which itself binds to the enzyme. The shared lowest common ancestors between Itraconazole and clotrimazole, as well as between azoles and Cyp3a7, further support a broader regulatory mechanism involving antifungal agents and their interaction with Cyp3a7. The evidence highlights a potential dependency on antifungal compounds to modulate Cyp3a7 activity, aligning with the role of Cyp3a7 in drug metabolism.",
